  "summary": "The paper proposes a variational Quantum Graph Neural Network (QGNN) for credit‑card fraud detection and evaluates it on the ULB/Kaggle dataset (284,807 transactions). On a simulator using 6 qubits and one VQC layer, the QGNN achieves 94.5% accuracy and F1=0.86 with AUC‑PR≈0.85, compared with a classical GraphSAGE baseline achieving 92.3% accuracy and F1=0.83.",
